      "title": "GATE EC — EDC | Semiconductor Physics & Carrier Transport",
      "subject": "Electronic Devices (EDC)",
      "subjectSlug": "edc",
      "topic": "Semiconductor Physics & Carrier Transport",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "question": "<p>The Einstein relation relating carrier diffusion coefficient $D$ and carrier mobility $\\mu$ in a semiconductor at thermal equilibrium temperature $T$ is:</p>",
      "options": [
        "$\\frac{D}{\\mu} = \\frac{k T}{q} = V_t$",
        "$\\frac{D}{\\mu} = \\frac{q}{k T}$",
        "$D \\cdot \\mu = \\frac{k T}{q}$",
        "$\\frac{\\mu}{D} = \\frac{k T}{q}$"
      ],
      "structuredOptions": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$\\frac{D}{\\mu} = \\frac{k T}{q} = V_t$",
          "html": "$\\frac{D}{\\mu} = \\frac{k T}{q} = V_t$"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$\\frac{D}{\\mu} = \\frac{q}{k T}$",
          "html": "$\\frac{D}{\\mu} = \\frac{q}{k T}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$D \\cdot \\mu = \\frac{k T}{q}$",
          "html": "$D \\cdot \\mu = \\frac{k T}{q}$"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$\\frac{\\mu}{D} = \\frac{k T}{q}$",
          "html": "$\\frac{\\mu}{D} = \\frac{k T}{q}$"
        }
      ],
      "answer": [
        "A"
      ],
      "tolerance": null,
      "marks": 1,
      "negativeMarks": 0.33,
      "explanation": "<div class='space-y-2'><p><strong>Step-by-Step Solution (Electronic Devices (EDC)):</strong></p><p>Einstein's relation: $\\frac{D_n}{\\mu_n} = \\frac{D_p}{\\mu_p} = \\frac{k T}{q} = V_t$ (thermal voltage $\\approx 26\\text{ mV}$ at $300\\text{ K}$).</p></div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "gate-ec-edc-q2",
      "testId": "gate-subject-ece-edc",
      "year": 2024,
      "orderIndex": 2,
      "section": "EC",
      "title": "GATE EC — EDC | PN Junction Diodes & Zener Diodes",
      "subject": "Electronic Devices (EDC)",
      "subjectSlug": "edc",
      "topic": "PN Junction Diodes & Zener Diodes",
      "type": "NAT",
      "question": "<p>An abrupt Silicon $p\\text{-}n$ junction has built-in potential $V_{bi} = 0.8\\text{ V}$. The transition capacitance at zero bias is $C_{j0} = 20\\text{ pF}$. When reverse biased with $V_R = 3.2\\text{ V}$, the junction capacitance $C_j = \\frac{C_{j0}}{\\sqrt{1 + V_R / V_{bi}}}$ (in $\\text{pF}$) is ________.</p>",
      "options": [],
      "structuredOptions": [],
      "answer": [
        "8.94"
      ],
      "tolerance": {
        "min": 8.7,
        "max": 9.2
      },
      "marks": 2,
      "negativeMarks": 0,
      "explanation": "<div class='space-y-2'><p><strong>Step-by-Step Solution (Electronic Devices (EDC)):</strong></p><p>$C_j = \\frac{20}{\\sqrt{1 + 3.2/0.8}} = \\frac{20}{\\sqrt{1 + 4}} = \\frac{20}{\\sqrt{5}} = \\frac{20}{2.236} \\approx 8.94\\text{ pF}$.</p></div>"
    },
